## FFD problems

As we step through the FFD, two problems are apparent:

1. We can't estimate the derivative for our last data point!

:::{.fragment}
  For a dataset with $n$ points, FFD will give us $n-1$ estimates of the derivative.
:::

2. The estimate seems inaccurate in several places.

:::{.fragment}
Let's address issue 2 first
:::

## Central finite difference

In the central finite difference (CFD) method, from a given pair of points, $(x_i,y_i)$,
we approximate the derivative by looking at the *two* pairs of points on either side: $(x_{i-1},y_{i-1})$ *and* $(x_{i+1},y_{i+1})$

:::{.fragment}
$$ \left[\frac{dy}{dx}\right]_i = \frac{y_{i+1} - y_{i-1}}{x_{i+1} - x_{i-1}}$$
:::

