## Differentiating with Numpy {.smaller}

Numpy has a function for discrete differentiation: `numpy.gradient`

::: {#55b36afa .cell output-location='fragment' execution_count=6}
``` {.python .cell-code code-line-numbers="4"}
dx = 0.05
x = np.arange(0,2*np.pi,dx)
y = np.sin(x)
dydx = np.gradient(y,x) # This should give an approx. derivative of sin(x)
```
:::


